  "basis": "The pie chart titled 'Global Energy Consumption by Source' explicitly labels each segment with its percentage share: Nuclear (45%), Hydroelectric (30%), Fossil Fuels (15%), and Renewables (10%). These percentages sum to 100% and are visually proportional to the slice areas, confirming they represent the intended consumption shares. The largest share is Nuclear at 45%. The routing criterion requires selecting the category with the greatest share for priority monitoring. The option 'Escalate Nuclear for priority source monitoring' is available and directly corresponds to the Nuclear category.",
